## Why This Is Asked
This problem tests DP formulation for selecting multiple non-overlapping subarrays with reconstruction—a common pattern in budget allocation and resource optimization scenarios.

## Key Concepts
- **DP over prefixes and block counts**: State `dp[i][t]` tracks the optimal solution using only the first i elements for exactly t blocks.
- **Prefix sums**: Enable O(1) computation of any subarray sum as `pref[r] - pref[l-1]`.
- **Backpointers**: Store decision history to reconstruct the actual subarray boundaries after computing the DP table.
- **Time/space complexity**: Baseline O(n²k) time and O(nk) space; can be optimized with divide-and-conquer or convex hull tricks for larger inputs.

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) pref[i] = pref[i - 1] + A[i - 1];

  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => new Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
  const choice = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => new Array(k + 1).fill(null));
  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      dp[i][t] = dp[i - 1][t];
      choice[i][t] = { type: 'skip', i: i - 1 };

      for (let s = 1; s <= i; s++) {
        const val = dp[s - 1][t - 1] + pref[i] - pref[s - 1];
        if (val > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = val;
          choice[i][t] = { type: 'start', s, i };
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct boundaries
  const blocks = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
    const c = choice[i][t];
    if (c.type === 'start') {
      blocks.unshift([c.s, c.i]);
      i = c.s - 1;
    } else {
      i = c.i;
    }
    t--;
  }

  return { maxSum: dp[n][k], boundaries: blocks };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design a DP for a non-standard segment value (length times segment max) with exact-k partitioning and path reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- 2D DP: dp[i][t] stores best value for first i elements using t segments
- Transition: dp[i][t] = max over j of dp[j][t-1] + (i-j) * max(A[j+1..i])
- On-the-fly max: as j decreases, update max(A[j+1..i]) incrementally
- Reconstruction: parent[i][t] stores last cut; backtrack to produce segments
- Complexity: O(n^2 k) time, O(nk) space

## Code Example
```javascript
function solve(A, n, k){
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=Math.min(i,k);t++){
      let maxv = -Infinity;
      for(let j=i-1;j>=t-1;j--){
        maxv = Math.max(maxv, A[j]); // adjust if 0-based/1-based indexing
        const val = dp[j][t-1] + (i-j) * maxv;
        if(val > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; par[i][t] = j; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruct
  let segments = [];
  let i=n, t=k;
  while(t>0){
    const j = par[i][t];
    segments.push([j+1, i]);
    i = j; t--;
  }
  segments.reverse();
  return {value: dp[n][k], segments};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to craft DP with interval constraints and reconstruction using palindromic substrings.

## Key Concepts
- Palindromic substring precomputation in O(n^2)
- DP over prefix length and exact count: dp[i][t]
- Transition considers ending a palindrome at i with start p
- Reconstruction requires backpointers to recover substrings

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPalSubstr(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const isPal = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(false));
  for (let i = n - 1; i >= 0; --i) {
    for (let j = i; j < n; ++j) {
      if (s[i] === s[j] && (j - i < 2 || isPal[i+1][j-1])) isPal[i][j] = true;
    }
  }
  const NEG = -1e9;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const par = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i][t], dp[i-1][t]);
      if (t > 0) {
        for (let p = 0; p < i; p++) {
          if (isPal[p][i-1]) {
            const val = dp[p][t-1] + (i - p);
            if (val > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = val; par[i][t] = p; }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // Reconstruction would trace par[] to extract substrings
}
```

