## Why This Is Asked

Tests dynamic programming on partitioning a string into numeric substrings, including numeric parsing and reconstruction, a common interview pattern.

## Key Concepts

- DP on string partitions with exact k blocks
- Efficient substring value computation and leading-zero handling
- Path reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time/space trade-offs: O(n^2 k) time, O(nk) space

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxSumPartition(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  // val[i][j] = value of s[i..j-1]
  const val = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => Array(n+1).fill(0));
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    if (s[i] === '0') { val[i][i+1] = 0; continue; }
    let cur = 0;
    for (let j = i; j < n; j++) {
      cur = cur*10 + (s.charCodeAt(j) - 48);
      val[i][j+1] = cur;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) dp[i][1] = val[0][i];
  for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
    for (let i = t; i <= n; i++) {
      for (let j = t-1; j < i; j++) {
        if (s[j] === '0' && i - j > 1) continue;
        const cand = dp[j][t-1] + val[j][i];
        if (cand > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = cand; par[i][t] = j; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruct cuts
  const cuts = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0) {
    const j = par[i][t];
    cuts.push(i);
    i = j;
    t--;
  }
  cuts.push(0);
  cuts.reverse();
  return { sum: dp[n][k], cuts };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt to allow at most k blocks instead of exactly k?
- How would you optimize for very large n or larger k (space/time optimizations, early pruning)?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests deriving a solvable DP for contiguous partitions with a length-based cost, plus a linear-time optimization and path reconstruction.

## Key Concepts

- Contiguous partition DP
- Prefix sums and O(nk) optimization
- Backtracking to report segment endpoints

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxTotalWithCost(A, k, c) {
  const n = A.length;
  const S = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) S[i] = S[i-1] + A[i-1];
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
    let bestVal = -Infinity, bestIdx = -1;
    for (let i = t; i <= n; i++) {
      const j = i - 1;
      if (dp[j][t-1] > -Infinity) {
        const cand = dp[j][t-1] - S[j] + c * j;
        if (cand > bestVal) { bestVal = cand; bestIdx = j; }
      }
      if (bestVal > -Infinity) {
        dp[i][t] = S[i] - c * i + c + bestVal;
        par[i][t] = bestIdx;
      }
    }
  }
  const segments = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  if (dp[n][k] <= -Infinity/2) return {best: -Infinity, segments: []};
  while (t > 0) {
    const j = par[i][t];
    segments.push([j+1, i]);
    i = j; t--;
  }
  segments.reverse();
  return {best: dp[n][k], segments};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt if c is paid only for non-first element or per segment boundary?
- How would you extend to maximize total value for at most k segments instead of exactly k?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests comprehensive DP design for partitioning problems with nonlinear segment costs involving both min and sum operations, requiring careful handling of base cases and path reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-dimensional DP over partition indices
- Range minimum query optimization within transitions
- Complete solution from base cases through reconstruction
- Space-time tradeoffs and optimization strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Initialize DP table and parent pointers
dp[0][0] = 0;
for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
  dp[i][1] = rangeMin(1, i) * prefix[i];
  parent[i][1] = 0;
}

// Fill DP table
for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
  for (let i = t; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let p = t-1; p < i; p++) {
      const segVal = rangeMin(p+1, i) * (prefix[i] - prefix[p]);
      const total = dp[p][t-1] + segVal;
      if (total > dp[i][t]) {
        dp[i][t] = total;
        parent[i][t] = p;
      }
    }
  }
}

// Reconstruct segments
let i = n, t = k;
while (t > 0) {
  const p = parent[i][t];
  segments[t] = [p+1, i];
  i = p;
  t--;
}
```

